The Voidheart was an orb about two feet across, lit from within with a violet glow and cased in overlapping dark scales that kept shifting under the hand. It hung where it was set, held by a heavy inertia that resisted being moved and carried it on once it was.

Standing near it felt like standing in the fane of a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]], though the place it belonged to lay on the far side of a tear in the [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]], past a room that mirrored a room of the real world. There it hung above a great hand that had pulled itself out of the ground, and the void-things around it crawled toward it.

The Party brought it out through the tear that opened over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor. Half of it was broken down and fed to the Heart [[Org/Iconoclasm/Eerie|Eerie]], which kept a seed of its magic-dampening nature; the orb itself is gone.
